# Prettier formats every other file with .prettierrc.json, and skips what
# .gitignore lists; CONTRIBUTING.md says how its settings were chosen. Left
# alone:
# build output, and the agent twins and llms.txt build-agent-twins.mjs writes,
dist/
agents/
llms.txt
coverage/
# vendored snapshots, which their producers format,
vendor/
web/vendor/
# the lockfile, which npm writes,
package-lock.json
# the guides, their images and navigation, published with the package as written,
content/
# Markdown, whose hand-wrapped prose and tables Prettier would rewrite,
*.md
# shell.html, a Go html/template whose actions sit inside tags and attributes,
shell.html
# and CSS, written one rule per line, which Prettier would expand rule by rule
# (serve.go also inlines styles.css and footer.css into every served page).
*.css
